# Cross-Platform Application Development Rules
# =============================================
# This file enforces the standard directory structure and development conventions
# for cross-platform applications built with React, Vite, Electron, and Capacitor.

## Project Structure

The project follows a **shared source architecture** where all platform apps import
from a common `src/` directory. Each platform adds only its native shell and
platform-specific overrides.

### Required Directory Structure

```
{project-root}/
├── app.config.json          # Application configuration (REQUIRED)
├── build.py                 # Unified build script (REQUIRED)
├── package.json             # Root package.json for shared dependencies
├── README.md                # Project documentation
├── .gitignore               # Git ignore rules
│
├── src/                     # SHARED SOURCE (all platforms import from here)
│   ├── App.jsx              # Main app component
│   ├── main.jsx             # Web entry point (BrowserRouter)
│   ├── index.css            # Base styles & theme variables
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── features/        # Feature components
│   │   ├── layout/          # Layout components
│   │   └── ui/              # Reusable UI components
│   ├── pages/               # Page components
│   ├── store/               # Zustand state stores
│   ├── hooks/               # React hooks
│   ├── context/             # React contexts
│   ├── utils/               # Utility functions
│   ├── extensions/          # Editor extensions (if applicable)
│   └── assets/              # Shared assets
│
├── public/                  # Shared public assets
│   ├── favicon.png
│   ├── logo-192.png
│   └── vite.svg
│
├── app-web/                 # Web platform
├── app-android/             # Android platform (Capacitor)
├── app-ios/                 # iOS platform (Capacitor)
├── app-macos/               # macOS platform (Electron)
├── app-windows/             # Windows platform (Electron)
│
├── plans/                   # Design documents & plans
├── logos/                   # Brand assets
└── .github/                 # GitHub Actions workflows
```

### Platform App Structure (Each app-{platform}/)

```
app-{platform}/
├── .gitignore               # Platform-specific git ignores
├── .env.example             # Environment variables template
├── index.html               # Entry HTML document
├── package.json             # Dependencies & npm scripts
├── vite.config.{js|ts}      # Vite build configuration
├── README.md                # Platform-specific documentation
│
├── config/                  # Platform-specific configuration
├── scripts/                 # Shell scripts (setup.sh, run.sh, build.sh)
├── src/                     # Platform-specific source code
│   ├── main.jsx             # Entry point (platform-specific router)
│   ├── index.css            # Platform CSS overrides
│   ├── hooks/               # Platform-specific hooks
│   ├── utils/               # Platform-specific utilities
│   └── native/              # Native bridge code
├── public/                  # Static assets
└── build/                   # Build resources (icons, signing configs)
```

## Conventions & Rules

### 1. Router Selection by Platform

| Platform Type | Router | Reason |
|---------------|--------|--------|
| Web (browser) | `BrowserRouter` | Standard browser history API |
| Mobile (Capacitor) | `MemoryRouter` | WebView doesn't support History API |
| Desktop (Electron) | `HashRouter` | `file://` protocol in production |

### 2. Vite Alias Conventions

| Platform Type | Alias | Resolves To |
|---------------|-------|-------------|
| Capacitor (Android, iOS) | `@` | `../src/` |
| Electron (macOS, Windows) | `@web` | `../src/` |
| Web | `@` | `../src/` |

### 3. Package Deduplication (CRITICAL)

Every `vite.config.{js|ts}` MUST include:
```javascript
resolve: {
  dedupe: ['react', 'react-dom', 'react-router-dom', 'zustand'],
}
```

### 4. CSS Import Chain

Every platform's `index.css` MUST:
1. Import shared base styles: `@import "../../src/index.css";`
2. Declare Tailwind source scanning: `@source "../../src";`
3. Add platform-specific overrides AFTER the imports

### 5. File Placement Rules

- **Shared code** → `src/` (project root) — NEVER duplicate into platform apps
- **Platform entry point** → `app-{platform}/src/main.jsx`
- **Platform CSS** → `app-{platform}/src/index.css`
- **Platform config** → `app-{platform}/config/`
- **Shell scripts** → `app-{platform}/scripts/`
- **Native bridge code** → `app-{platform}/src/native/`
- **Build resources** → `app-{platform}/build/`
- **Static assets** → `app-{platform}/public/`

### 6. Naming Conventions

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Platform directory | `app-{platform}` | `app-android`, `app-macos` |
| Package name | `{appname}-{platform}` | `myapp-android`, `myapp-macos` |
| Config directory | `config/` | `config/capacitor.config.json` |
| Scripts directory | `scripts/` | `scripts/setup.sh` |
| Native code directory | `src/native/` | `src/native/main.ts` |

