## Build Commands

Use `./build.py` for all build operations:

```bash
# Web
./build.py web:setup     # Initial setup
./build.py web:dev       # Development server
./build.py web:build     # Production build

# Android
./build.py android:setup # Initial setup
./build.py android:run   # Run on device
./build.py android:apk   # Build APK

# iOS
./build.py ios:setup     # Initial setup
./build.py ios:run       # Run on simulator
./build.py ios:xcode     # Open in Xcode

# macOS
./build.py mac:setup     # Initial setup
./build.py mac:dev       # Development mode
./build.py mac:dmg       # Build DMG (falls back to ZIP if needed)

# Windows
./build.py win:setup     # Initial setup
./build.py win:dev       # Development mode
./build.py win:nsis      # Build NSIS installer
```

## Quick Checklist for New Platforms

- [ ] Create directory structure following the template
- [ ] Configure Vite alias pointing to shared `src/`
- [ ] Add `resolve.dedupe` for all stateful libraries
- [ ] Add `@source` directive for Tailwind
- [ ] Create platform-specific entry point (`main.jsx`)
- [ ] Create platform-specific CSS with imports
- [ ] Add platform to `app.config.json`
- [ ] Add commands to `build.py` if needed

## Reference Documentation

For detailed component APIs, hook usage, utility functions, and platform setup instructions,
see `docs/app-guide.md`. This documentation travels with every app created from this template.

### Available Built-in Modules

| Category | Location | Contents |
|----------|----------|----------|
| UI Components | `src/components/ui/` | Button, Modal, Toast, Loading |
| Layout | `src/components/layout/` | AppLayout, ErrorBoundary |
| Hooks | `src/hooks/` | useLocalStorage, useMediaQuery, useDebounce |
| Store | `src/store/` | useAppStore (Zustand with persistence) |
| Utilities | `src/utils/` | api, storage, validation, format, platform |
| Config | `src/config/` | app, constants, env |
| Context | `src/context/` | ThemeContext |

When building features, **prefer using these built-in modules** over adding new dependencies.
Import UI components via barrel export: `import { Button, Modal } from '@/components/ui';`
